30,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The billing is based on area, not heads. Empty desks still cost us 41,000 yen monthly.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Minato,,The printer row is nine decibels louder. My chair needs days to adjust properly.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,Moving desks takes four to nine minutes per person. Last year's shuffles took two weeks.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The plan gives four desks windows, but three are on the wall. Arrival times vary wildly.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"When we sat close last spring, we stopped writing notes. New hires learn by listening.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@May, that transition time is significant. We need to minimize disruption.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, if the window seats are fixed, who gets them? It feels unfair.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, if we rotate, we avoid the ""bad seat"" resentment, but the setup time adds up.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Daisuke, listening is valuable, but we can't rely on chance for collaboration.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minato, I agree. Comfort is key, but so is not being stuck in a noisy spot.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"The facilities quote is 6,200 yen per desk for re-running power. Every change costs money.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Minato,,"So if we move often, the cost and the physical adjustment both hurt.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"Fixed desks mean no setup time, but we lock in the bad spots permanently.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Free address solves the fairness issue, but the arrival time data shows it's a race.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"If we rotate blocks, we share the good and bad spots, but we lose the listening benefit.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,We need a balance. Fixed is expensive to change. Free is chaotic. Rotating might be the middle.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Minato,,Rotating blocks means I get a new chair every few months. That's hard on my body.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"But it prevents the ""lucky"" and ""unlucky"" seats. And we can plan the moves.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I can live with rotation if the intervals are long enough to settle in.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I think rotation helps me connect with different people. I'm okay with the change.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Option A is fixed. Option B is rotating blocks. Option C is free address.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I'm leaning towards B, but I'm worried about the physical adjustment time.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,B seems best for fairness. We can schedule the moves to minimize downtime.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,C is too chaotic given the arrival times. A is too rigid. B is the compromise.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I prefer B. It lets me sit with different people and share the good spots.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Minato, the physio note says adjustments take days. Rotation might be too frequent.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Minato,,"If we rotate quarterly, maybe it's manageable? I don't want to move every month.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"Quarterly sounds reasonable. It's long enough to settle, short enough to share.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,Agreed. Quarterly rotation balances fairness with stability.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I'm happy with quarterly. It feels fair and keeps the team connected.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Victoria,,The cost of re-running power is a one-time hit per move. Quarterly means four moves a year.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Minato,,I'll try to keep my chair settings consistent across desks if possible.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"That's 24,800 yen in facilities costs. Plus the time cost. But it's less than the empty desk waste.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"The empty desk waste is 41,000 yen a month. We can't afford to keep wasting that.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I think we should go with B. It addresses the fairness and connection issues.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I agree. B is the most rational choice given the constraints.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Minato,,Okay. I'll do my best to adapt.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,Let's vote. I'm for B.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'm for B.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'm for B.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
